# HashSucker environment configuration
# Copy to .env, fill the values below, then: docker compose up -d
#
# Most users change only ~5 values: TORBOX_API_KEY plus the two HOST PATHS.
# Everything else is OPTIONAL (feature disabled when absent) or CONDITIONAL
# (required only when its feature is enabled). Secrets stay blank here.
# Conventions: REQUIRED CORE blocks startup when missing (compose :? or a
# clear not_ready); OPTIONAL absent disables its feature; OPTIONAL
# partially configured is an explicit config error, never silent behavior.

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# RELEASES (normal users: leave these alone)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Image channels (one Compose file serves all three):
#   HASHSUCKER_VERSION=latest   stable releases only (moves on v* tags)
#   HASHSUCKER_VERSION=main     continuous dogfood (every main commit)
#   HASHSUCKER_VERSION=v0.1.0   explicitly pinned (immutable)
#   HASHSUCKER_VERSION=sha-<x>  exact-commit reproducibility
# `docker compose pull && docker compose up -d` consumes published images
# — no local toolchain needed. Developers building from source use
# `docker compose build` / `up --build` (same file).
# HASHSUCKER_VERSION=latest
# Registry override (only if mirroring images elsewhere).
# HASHSUCKER_REGISTRY=ghcr.io/peedubyah
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# HOST PATHS
# These are the only paths most users should need to change.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Private state root (survives container recreation; back this up):
# discovery + control-plane SQLite, request queue, importer state,
# download staging. Grows over time (corpus DB + control plane).
# Losing this loses corpus, handoffs, library, and prepared state.
# Unraid example: HASHSUCKER_DATA_PATH=/mnt/user/appdata/hashsucker
# Ownership: container processes run as PUID:PGID (defaults 99:100 —
# Unraid nobody:users). The data path must be writable by that user.
HASHSUCKER_DATA_PATH=./hy4-data

# Consumer-visible media root (this is the path Plex/Jellyfin must see):
# published .strm files live in <MEDIA_PATH>/strm. Point Plex/Jellyfin
# at this host path (exact same files, any mount point inside them).
# Grows slowly (tiny text files). No backup needed (regenerable).
# This root NEVER stores media bytes: promotion uses its own root below.
# Unraid example: HASHSUCKER_MEDIA_PATH=/mnt/user/media/hashsucker
HASHSUCKER_MEDIA_PATH=./hy4-media

# Owned-storage root for permanent promotion output (optional, off by
# default). POST /api/library/:id/promote materializes one exact
# TorrentFile here as a real media file you own. Set this to the
# container path of your permanent media (default mount is /permanent,
# backed by HASHSUCKER_PERMANENT_HOST_PATH) to enable promotion; leave
# unset and the promote API refuses while everything else works
# unchanged.
# This is a genuine human storage decision, not tuning: bytes here are
# owned media (back them up per your normal media policy), NOT cache
# (hy4-cache stays disposable) and NOT regenerable (unlike STRM).
# Unraid example: HASHSUCKER_PERMANENT_PATH=/permanent
# HASHSUCKER_PERMANENT_PATH=
# Host path backing /permanent (created empty; inert until the var above
# is set). Unraid example:
# HASHSUCKER_PERMANENT_HOST_PATH=/mnt/user/media/owned
# HASHSUCKER_PERMANENT_HOST_PATH=./hy4-permanent

# Staging/output root for generic download intents (optional, off by
# default). POST /api/download-request stages verified bytes here for
# external importers (Requestrr, Sonarr/Radarr, manual moves):
# <root>/movies/Title (Year)/... and <root>/tv/Series/Season XX/...
# Set to the container path of your staging area (/download, backed by
# HASHSUCKER_DOWNLOAD_HOST_PATH) to enable; leave unset and the API
# refuses while everything else works unchanged. HashSucker stops at the
# staged file and never touches whatever library path an importer moves
# it into.
# Unraid example: HASHSUCKER_DOWNLOAD_PATH=/download
# HASHSUCKER_DOWNLOAD_PATH=
# HASHSUCKER_DOWNLOAD_HOST_PATH=./hy4-downloads

# Explicit single-mount overrides (rarely needed — the two roots above
# plus the download/permanent host paths derive every mount). Set one
# ONLY to place that mount outside its default (e.g. queue on a
# different filesystem). Unset = derived, always consistent between
# media-search and the importer. Precedence per mount is fixed:
# explicit HASHSUCKER_*_HOST_PATH > HASHSUCKER_DATA_PATH /
# HASHSUCKER_MEDIA_PATH-derived default > legacy alias >
# repo-local fallback. In particular a set DATA/MEDIA root always beats
# a legacy alias — legacy aliases only apply when neither the explicit
# override nor its root is set (this keeps old installs working while
# making migration to the new roots unambiguous).
# HASHSUCKER_DISCOVERY_HOST_PATH=
# HASHSUCKER_QUEUE_HOST_PATH=
# HASHSUCKER_STRM_HOST_PATH=
# HASHSUCKER_TORBOX_IMPORTER_HOST_PATH=
# HASHSUCKER_TORBOX_IMPORTER_DOWNLOADS_HOST_PATH=
# Leaf rule: every canonical HASHSUCKER_*_HOST_PATH above is the FINAL host
# directory that gets mounted (compose never appends to it). Point each at
# the real leaf directory (e.g. the dir containing discovery-cache.db, not
# its parent). Roots (HASHSUCKER_DATA_PATH / HASHSUCKER_MEDIA_PATH) are the
# opposite: compose appends the leaf (/discovery, /queue, /strm,
# /torbox-importer, /downloads). Legacy aliases behave like roots, so a
# legacy value that already names a leaf double-appends unless shadowed by
# the matching canonical pin — that exact misconfiguration once pointed
# media-search at empty state.
# Legacy aliases (still honored; new names win). Prefer the names above.
# DISCOVERY_HOST_PATH=
# REQUESTS_HOST_PATH=
# STRM_HOST_PATH=
# TORBOX_IMPORTER_HOST_PATH=
# DOWNLOADS_HOST_PATH=
# DOWNLOAD_HOST_PATH=
# PERMANENT_HOST_PATH=

# =============================================================================
# Core (REQUIRED: at least one debrid provider)
# =============================================================================
# Choose one or both. One healthy configured provider is a READY system;
# neither configured is NOT_READY. No dummy values needed for the absent one.
# TorBox API key. Enables TorBox discovery, binding, serving, and inventory.
TORBOX_API_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# Providers (at least one of TorBox / Real-Debrid REQUIRED; rest OPTIONAL)
# =============================================================================
# Real-Debrid API key. Enables RD discovery, RD binding benchmark
# data, and RD-backed serving. Absent = TorBox-only operation.
# (The TorBox importer service idles without TORBOX_API_KEY; Arr jobs
# needing it fail fast per-job, never silently.)
REALDEBRID_API_KEY=

# Optional TorBox API base override, primarily for isolated testing.
# TORBOX_API_URL=https://api.torbox.app/v1/api

# Torrentio needs no configuration: its manifest URL is derived from the
# provider keys at runtime. (The TORRENTIO_*_MANIFEST_URL variables some
# old guides mention are not read by any service.)

# Comet manifests (OPTIONAL live-discovery sources).
COMET_TORBOX_MANIFEST_URL=
COMET_REALDEBRID_MANIFEST_URL=

# Torznab endpoints (OPTIONAL; JSON array of {id, name, url, role, enabled, sortOrder}).
TORZNAB_URLS=

# Prowlarr (OPTIONAL candidate intelligence; sensors only, never fulfillment).
# Only these two are needed — no tracker credentials, no indexer definitions.
PROWLARR_URL=
PROWLARR_API_KEY=

# Cinemeta base URL (OPTIONAL, defaults to https://v3-cinemeta.strem.io).
# CINEMETA_BASE_URL=

# =============================================================================
# Publication (STRM root derives from HASHSUCKER_MEDIA_PATH above)
# =============================================================================
# STRM output is <HASHSUCKER_MEDIA_PATH>/strm unless HASHSUCKER_STRM_HOST_PATH is set.
# (Unraid: put HASHSUCKER_MEDIA_PATH on your media share, e.g.
# /mnt/user/media/hashsucker — NOT on appdata — so Plex/Jellyfin libraries
# can include it. Data-plane cache stays internal via the hy4-cache volume.)

# Public base URL baked into .strm files (edge endpoint). Defaults to
# http://localhost:8080; set to the LAN/reverse-proxy URL on Unraid.
# HASHSUCKER_BASE_URL=

# =============================================================================
# Corpus (all OPTIONAL; safe defaults keep a fresh deploy self-sufficient)
# =============================================================================
# First run is polite by design: the corpus builds in bounded background
# sessions (~1000 fragments / ~4 min each, then a short pause), checkpoints
# after every fragment, and resumes across restarts. Requests work from
# minute one (live sources carry) while diagnostics reports
# state=usable-partial + progress until the baseline completes (~1h wall).
# Corpus maintenance master switch. Unset/1 = bootstrap when absent + update
# on cadence. Set 0 to disable (discovery stays live-only).
# CORPUS_MAINTENANCE=
# Bootstrap a blank data directory automatically. Unset/1 = yes.
# CORPUS_AUTO_BOOTSTRAP=
# Update cadence in hours (default 6, aligned to upstream sync; min 0.5).
# CORPUS_UPDATE_INTERVAL_HOURS=
# Upstream hashlist repo (default debridmediamanager/hashlists).
# CORPUS_DMM_REPO=
# GitHub token for upstream API calls (OPTIONAL: raises rate limits for
# revision checks; fragment fetches use unauthenticated raw endpoints).
# CORPUS_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# =============================================================================
# Request ingress (all OPTIONAL; absent = no inbound requests accepted)
# =============================================================================
# Seerr webhook bearer token (CONDITIONAL: required to accept Seerr webhooks).
SEERR_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=
# Seerr server URL + API key (CONDITIONAL: required for TMDB→IMDb identity
# resolution and TV season enumeration; movies with IMDb IDs work without).
SEERR_URL=
SEERR_API_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# Consumers (all OPTIONAL; absent = no notification for that consumer)
# =============================================================================
# Jellyfin (CONDITIONAL: all three required to enable notifications).
JELLYFIN_URL=
JELLYFIN_API_KEY=
JELLYFIN_MEDIA_ROOT=
# Plex (CONDITIONAL: URL + token required for refresh; section IDs and roots
# default per library layout when set).
PLEX_URL=
PLEX_TOKEN=
PLEX_MOVIES_SECTION_ID=
PLEX_TV_SECTION_ID=
PLEX_MOVIES_ROOT=
PLEX_TV_ROOT=

# =============================================================================
# Anticipatory scheduler (all OPTIONAL; no seeded intents = fully inert)
# =============================================================================
# Master switch. Unset/1 = enabled; 0 disables prepare/publish ticks.
# ANTICIPATION_ENABLED=
# Tick cadence in minutes (default 15; min 1). One bounded intent per tick.
# FUTURE_INTENT_INTERVAL_MIN=
# Preparation window in days (default 30): far-future expectations sleep
# until the window instead of preparing early.
# ANTICIPATION_PREPARE_DAYS=
# Publication/prewarm window in days (default 7): consumer publication and
# the ~142 MB Plex prewarm wait until use is near. Preparation may run earlier.
# ANTICIPATION_PUBLISH_DAYS=

# =============================================================================
# Lifecycle (all OPTIONAL; safe defaults are conservative)
# =============================================================================
# Consumer reconcile + automatic retirement stay off unless enabled.
# CONSUMER_RECONCILE_ENABLED=
# RETIREMENT_ENABLED=

# =============================================================================
# Service bindings (OPTIONAL; loopback publishing is the default)
# =============================================================================
# Put an authenticated reverse proxy in front before using non-loopback.
MEDIA_SEARCH_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
MEDIA_SEARCH_PORT=3000
# EDGE_BIND_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0
# EDGE_PORT=8080

# Supplementary GID for queue filesystem access (Unraid: usually 100=users).
MEDIA_SEARCH_QUEUE_GID=100

# Metadata cache tuning (OPTIONAL; built-in defaults apply when unset).
# METADATA_CACHE_TTL_MS=300000
# METADATA_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES=500

# =============================================================================
# Physical acquisition importer (runs by default; idles cleanly without Arr)
# =============================================================================
# The importer boots with only TORBOX_API_KEY (queue polling + TorBox
# inventory). Arr endpoints are needed solely for physical Arr imports;
# without them those jobs fail fast and loudly per-job, never silently.
# Runtime user/group for importer container (Unraid: 99/100).
PUID=99
PGID=100

# Importer persistent state root on host (mounted at /config).
# Derived from HASHSUCKER_DATA_PATH by default; set explicitly ONLY to
# place it outside the data root.
# HASHSUCKER_TORBOX_IMPORTER_HOST_PATH=./hy4-data/torbox-importer

# Download staging area on host (needed only for physical imports;
# this is the importer's /downloads mount, not generic /download output).
# Derived from HASHSUCKER_DATA_PATH by default; set explicitly ONLY to
# place it outside the data root.
# HASHSUCKER_TORBOX_IMPORTER_DOWNLOADS_HOST_PATH=./hy4-data/downloads

# Polling interval in seconds (OPTIONAL).
POLL_INTERVAL=10

# Resolver profiler (ADVANCED; 1 enables per-resolution profiling).
# RESOLVER_PROFILE=0

# --- Radarr (CONDITIONAL: required only when the importer runs) ---
# Media-search also reads these for future-intent sensing (sensors only:
# no downloads, no queue changes). Neither set = Arr integration disabled.
# URL without key = degraded configuration error, never silent.
RADARR_URL=
RADARR_API_KEY=
RADARR_ROOT_FOLDER=/data/Movies
RADARR_PROFILE_HD=4
RADARR_PROFILE_4K_WEB=7
RADARR_PROFILE_4K_BLU=8

# --- Sonarr (CONDITIONAL: required only when the importer runs) ---
# Same sensor semantics as Radarr (calendar/monitored reads only).
SONARR_URL=
SONARR_API_KEY=
# Arr sync cadence in hours (default 6; min 0.5). Batch reconciliation:
# a few list/calendar calls per sync, never per-item polling.
# ARR_SYNC_INTERVAL_HOURS=
